// Point-cloud shape data for the hero particle field: two landmarks,
// Coliseo and Metropolis, each matched point-by-point against its exact
// reference image ("Coliseo en particulas.png", "Metropolis en
// particulas.png"). Nothing cropped out of either -- trees, ground and the
// drifting disintegration dust at the edges are all in the data, same as
// the source. Extraction: scipy.ndimage connected-component labeling on
// every non-white pixel; a real, visually-isolated dust mote keeps its
// exact centroid, and denser regions (stonework, shadow, sculpture) are
// re-expanded into k = round(blob_area / area_of_one_mote) points sampled
// from real ink pixels inside that blob's own mask, so no density is lost
// in the areas carrying the most detail. Each point's colour is the real
// RGB sampled from its source pixel, run through a contrast curve (pivot
// 0.60, contrast 1.55x, gamma 1.18 darkening) so shadow recesses and
// highlights read distinctly instead of the source's naturally soft
// tonality getting diluted further by sparse point rendering.
